    "result_text": "There's only one test file (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the email-uniqueness rule for owner creation:\n\n1. **New exception** `DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 extends the existing `OwnerConflictException` base (whose subclasses are all handled uniformly by `ExceptionControllerAdvice` as **409 Conflict**), with the client-facing detail `\"An owner with the same email already exists\"`.\n\n2. **Wired a new guard** into `OwnerRestControllerV1`:\n   - Added `rejectWhenEmailInUse(owner)` to the `rejectDisallowedOwnerCreation` chain, alongside the existing daily-limit, city-capacity, and telephone guards.\n   - The guard reuses the existing `isValueInUseByExistingOwner` helper with `Owner::getEmail` and `normalizeEmail` (lower-casing), so an owner is rejected when its lower-cased email already matches any existing owner's. Owners without an email (null) are unaffected, matching the helper's null-safe behaviour.\n\nThe email is already canonicalised to lower-case earlier in `normalizeOwnerFields`, so the comparison is case-insensitive as specified. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
